      "writtenOn": "2014-08-20T08:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, region URL is a URL at the SP side (where the SAML assertion will be sent). Normaly objects like sso_endpoint (also single_logout_service) are the endpoint where SP directs its SAML request, so it\u0027s at the IdP side (Where a SAML REQUEST should be sent). Refer to FIM idp_metadata.xml you had sent me couple of days ago to see a real-world examples.\nIt\u0027s empty by default cause I don\u0027t know how to reliably guess hostname without using wsgi.Application().",
